---
import Section from './Section.astro';

const INDEX_BYTES = 362121;
const ENGINE_BYTES = 4309;
const SRAM_BUDGET = 65536;

const share = (value: number) => `${((value / INDEX_BYTES) * 100).toFixed(2)}%`;

const bars = [
  {
    label: 'index on',
    bytes: INDEX_BYTES,
    value: '362,121 B',
    fill: 'bar__fill--index',
  },
  {
    label: '64 KB SRAM budget',
    bytes: SRAM_BUDGET,
    value: '65,536 B',
    fill: 'bar__fill--budget',
  },
  {
    label: 'index off',
    bytes: ENGINE_BYTES,
    value: '4,309 B',
    fill: 'bar__fill--engine',
  },
];

const measurements = [
  { what: 'Live peak heap, two facts and a read back', value: '4,309 bytes' },
  { what: 'Cumulative allocation over the round trip', value: '12,150 bytes' },
  { what: 'Largest single allocation', value: '760 bytes' },
  { what: 'Static SRAM used, inside a 64 KB budget', value: '32,812 bytes' },
  { what: 'Firmware text (flash)', value: '144,842 bytes' },
];

const latency = [
  { scale: '100,000 records', indexed: '25.4 to 26.3 µs', scan: '915 to 941 µs' },
  { scale: '1,000,000 records', indexed: '226.6 to 229.5 µs', scan: '18.6 to 19.4 ms' },
];
---

<Section
  id="proof"
  label="Proof"
  title="Running without an operating system is a measurement"
  lede="A firmware image boots in emulation on a RISC-V target with no operating system and no runtime, completes a write and a read, and peaks at 4,309 bytes of live heap."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      The largest single allocation in that round trip is 760 bytes, inside a 64 KB SRAM budget
      the build enforces. A second build compiles the C surface and runs the same test. Both run
      in continuous integration on every change.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="bars">
    {
      bars.map((bar) => (
        <div class:list={['bar', bar.label === 'index off' && 'bar--engine']}>
          <span class="bar__label">{bar.label}</span>
          <span class="bar__track">
            <span class:list={['bar__fill', bar.fill]} style={`width:${share(bar.bytes)}`} />
          </span>
          <span class="bar__value">{bar.value}</span>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <p class="note">
    Live peak heap for the MCU round trip with the structural index on and off, on one scale. The
    optional index costs about 354 KB of live heap, which is why the reference build leaves it
    off and keeps the engine in the 64 KB class.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Measurement</th>
          <th>Result</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          measurements.map((row) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="lead">{row.what}</td>
              <td class="num">{row.value}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3>Three-axis query latency</h3>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        A three-axis query over a one-day window answers in about 0.93 ms at 100,000 records and
        about 18.9 ms at one million, from the same structure that holds every other axis, and
        the cost grows with the number of records.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Scale</th>
          <th>Structural index</th>
          <th>Scan path</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          latency.map((row) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="lead">{row.scale}</td>
              <td class="num">{row.indexed}</td>
              <td class="num">{row.scan}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="note">
    Those figures come from a virtual test environment, a release build, and the median of ten
    samples from the Criterion harness. The device runs the same scan path. The on-target cost
    is not yet measured, and the scan path is the one the read path uses.
  </p>
</Section>

<style>
  .bar--engine .bar__label {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
